Pv4..\\b)`** — Starts at the beginning of a line and uses a positive lookahead to verify an IPv4 address exists somewhere on that line\n- **`.*\\b`** — Greedily matches characters up to a word boundary, which helps position us at a potential date\n- **`(...DATE...)`** — Capturing group matching the last valid date:\n  - Days 01-31 for months 01,03,05,07,08,10,12\n  - Days 01-30 for months 04,06,09,11  \n  - Days 01-29 for month 02 (February)\n- **`\\b(?!.*\\b..DATE..\\b)`** — Word boundary after the date with a negative lookahead ensuring no other valid date follows on the same line\n\nThe word boundaries prevent false matches like \"user 1134-12-1234\" (the day \"1234\" exceeds valid ranges, and the lookahead prevents matching within a longer number).","ttft_ms":102008,"type":"result","duration_ms":107193,"uuid":"b34ee17a-f268-4a04-9dfc-7342aa5f64ae","ttft_stream_ms":714,"time_to_request_ms":82,"queued_turn_count":0}
